    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0143" n="47" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg47"/>

                <head>No. 27.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Jay</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-02-05"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 5,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 199.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 402. of the 13th ultimo, in regard to the approaching Exposition at Vienna.
                    In reply, I <pb facs="0144" n="48" xml:id="pg48"/> have to state that the
                    subject-has been recommended to the consideration of Congress, by whom it is
                    regarded with favor, but, as yet, no appropriation has been made by that
                    body.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
